et_-_III_century_BC_-_Porta_Rosa_-_Velia_-_Italy.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":2400,"height":1600},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0e/Greek_street_-_III_century_BC_-_Porta_Rosa_-_Velia_-_Italy.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greek_street_-_III_century_BC_-_Porta_Rosa_-_Velia_-_Italy.JPG","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=33119461","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2013-03-17 19:39:13","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Greek street - III century BC - Porta Rosa - Velia - Italy","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Taken with Canon EOS 350D|Ancient Greek architecture in Italy|Self-published work|Via di Porta Rosa","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Greek street - IV-III century BC - Porta Rosa - Velia - Italy\nThe Porta Rosa road was the main street of <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Elea\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Elea\">Elea</a>. It connects the northern quarter with the southern quarter, through the viaduct called Porta Rosa. The street is 5 meters wide and has an incline of 18\u00a0% in the steepest part.  It is paved with limestone blocks, girders cut in square blocks, and on one side a small gutter for the drainage of rain water. The building is dated during the time of the reorganization of the city during Helenistic age (IV-III century BC)","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2008-08-08","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<span class=\"int-own-work\" lang=\"en\">Own work</span>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist